# tenshoe --input script: two pads, boot -> title -> main menu -> 2P VS -> selects -> race -> result.
# Steps are SysLib.frameCount (state.log F). Run 846 (agent-a); run 853 (agent-c): P2 needs its own
# board confirm (1500) before P1 picks the course; the race starts at ~1792 (flow 5,2,2).
# Plan 24 (agent-a): with the catch-up speed fixed (SnowBoarder_limitSpeed's pool constants) the port
# matches the N64 (n64ref) rider for rider over the whole script. Both ride straight with the stick up
# to 8000; P2 crashes out at ~6930 (health -2: P1 wins, race state 2 at 6933), the result times out and
# the next round starts at ~7638 (race state 1 again). port/tools/n64ref/vs2p-golden.tsv holds the
# N64's per-step rider positions for this script (modes-check.py compares them).
# END 7800
PADS 2
F 480:3 START          # title
F 560:3 A
F 620:3 DD
F 680:3 DD
F 740:3 DD
F 800:3 DD
F 860:3 A
F 1100:3 P1 A P2 A
F 1200:3 P1 A P2 A
F 1300:3 P1 A P2 A
F 1400:3 P1 A P2 A
F 1500:3 P2 A
F 1600:3 P1 A
F 1700:3 P1 A
F 1800:3 P1 A
F 1900-8000 P1 STICK 0,80 P2 STICK 0,80
